// ============================================================================
// poker-hand-counts.epher -- five-card hands: totals, flushes, big hands
//
// Counts hands with the ncr builtin (guide 1.13): the 52-card deck holds
// ncr(52, 5) = 2598960 five-card hands, of which 4 * ncr(13, 5) = 5148
// are flushes (five cards of one suit; the straight flushes are included,
// so 40 of those 5148 are straight flushes and 4 of the 40 are royal).
//
// The probability of a flush is 4 * ncr(13, 5) / ncr(52, 5) = 33/16660
// exactly, about 0.00198, or one hand in 505. The fraction and the
// computed quotient are cross-checked below with exact arithmetic.
//
// Source: Feller, "An Introduction to Probability Theory and Its
// Applications", volume 1, chapter 2. The counts are exact integers.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/counting/poker-hand-counts.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
// ============================================================================

// ---- results ----
// The total number of five-card hands: 52 choose 5.
ncr(52, 5)

// Flushes: pick the suit (4 ways), then 5 of its 13 ranks.
4 * ncr(13, 5)
print("hands:", ncr(52, 5), "of which", 4 * ncr(13, 5), "are flushes")

// The flush probability, with the exact fraction 33/16660.
print("P(flush):", 4 * ncr(13, 5) / ncr(52, 5))
4 * ncr(13, 5) / ncr(52, 5) == 33 / 16660
print("hands per flush, about:", round(ncr(52, 5) / (4 * ncr(13, 5))))

// Two rarer families inside the flush count: 40 straight flushes (10
// rank runs per suit) and, among them, the 4 royal flushes.
print("straight flushes:", 10 * 4)
print("royal flushes:", 4)

// Two more classic counts: four of a kind (13 ranks, all 4 suits, plus
// any fifth card) and full houses (rank for the triple, rank for the
// pair: 13 * 4 * 12 * ncr(4, 2) = 3744).
print("four of a kind:", 13 * ncr(48, 1))
print("full houses:", 13 * ncr(4, 3) * 12 * ncr(4, 2))

// The categories above are disjoint, so they can be checked against the
// total only together with the hands left over; the flush probability
// itself is the anchor: 5148 / 2598960 = 33/16660 exactly.
// ---- expected output ----
// = 2598960
// = 5148
// = hands: 2598960 of which 5148 are flushes
// = P(flush): 0.00198079231693
// = true
// = hands per flush, about: 505
// = straight flushes: 40
// = royal flushes: 4
// = four of a kind: 624
// = full houses: 3744
